  "findings": [
    {
      "description": "Password hashing is reverted to MD5, a cryptographically insecure hash, conflicting with the existing merged security fix that requires bcrypt. MD5 is fast and collision-prone, making password storage vulnerable to brute-force and tampering. The verify_password function also compares unsalted MD5 digests. This must not be merged in its current form.",
      "category": "other",
      "severity": "critical"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "REJECT",
  "fix_description": "Remove the MD5 implementation and restore the already-merged bcrypt-based fix. Update hash_password to use bcrypt.hashpw with a salt: import bcrypt; return bcrypt.hashpw(password.encode(), bcrypt.gensalt()). Update verify_password to compare the stored bcrypt hash using bcrypt.checkpw(password.encode(), hashed.encode() if hashed is bytes else hashed). This aligns the PR with the existing security fix and avoids the merge conflict. If bcrypt is not yet a declared dependency, add it to the project dependencies as part of the fix.",
